config.nether_api.initialDragon=Automatic Ender Dragon
config.nether_api.initialDragon.tooltip=The End dimension creates an Ender Dragon when it's first loaded. An End Gateway is automatically created if this setting is disabled, to still allow exploration of the outer end islands.
config.nether_api.initialSpawnDim=Player Spawn Dimension
config.nether_api.initialSpawnDim.tooltip=The default spawn dimension for players. This is only used for players without a spawn point.
config.nether_api.respawnDims=Player Respawn Dimension Overrides
config.nether_api.respawnDims.tooltip=Allows additional dimensions (aside from the Overworld) to allow or deny players (without a spawn point there) from respawning within them. By default, the Overworld allows respawning and the End & Nether don't (they kick you back to the "Player Spawn Dimension" when you die). §rHere's an example config entry: §o{DimId: 1, Respawn: true}§r
config.nether_api.tallNether=Tall Nether §lHOVER OVER ME!
config.nether_api.tallNether.tooltip=Generate the Nether with a height of 256. §4WARNING: Only enable this feature for new worlds (or old worlds if you reset the Nether first)! This feature can cause additional world generation lag, so if you experience any performance issues, it's recommended to install the following mods: §oAlfheim Lighting Engine, CensoredASM, Nothirium, and VintageFix. §r§cNote: For many mods that generate their own nether features, you'll have to adjust their configs to account for the new height. Currently all mods with builtin support (and do not require manual config editing) are as follows: §oBetterNether, Biomes O' Plenty, Journey Into The Light, Natura, Nethercraft Classic, and NetherEx. It's also assumed that any mods using Nether API as a dependency have automatic support for this feature.§r

